[E-TAILREC] Error: `double` is marked @[tailrec], but a recursive call isn't in tail position
   ╭─[ reject/tailrec-constructor.sw:9:28 ]
   │
 9 │   | [x, ..xs] => [x * 2, ..double xs]
   │                            ────┬────  
   │                                ╰────── its result goes into a field of `Cons`, which is built after it returns
   │ 
   │ Note 1: a call is in tail position when its result is the function's result, with nothing left to do after it returns; then each call is a turn of a loop, not a new frame
   │ 
   │ Note 2: building a list or a tree around the call is cheap on `stitchwort run` and in JavaScript, but @[tailrec] promises only true tail calls: carry the result in an extra parameter and reverse it at the end
───╯
